## Players

Player identities and recorded playing positions. Join using player_id, not surname.

### Data Properties

| Name | Display Name | Type | Description | Mapped Field |
|------|--------------|------|-------------|--------------|
| key_id | Row Key | integer | Source row key; not a person, team or tournament identity. | key_id |
| player_id | Player ID | string | Stable player identifier; join using this value. | player_id |
| family_name | Family Name | string | Recorded family name; use the person ID to identify a unique individual. | family_name |
| given_name | Given Name | string | Recorded given name, preserving source spelling and accents. | given_name |
| birth_date | Birth Date | string | Recorded birth date in YYYY-MM-DD format. | birth_date |
| female | Female Player | integer | 1 for a female player, otherwise 0. | female |
| goal_keeper | Goalkeeper | integer | 1 when goalkeeper is a recorded playing position, otherwise 0. | goal_keeper |
| defender | Defender | integer | 1 when defender is a recorded playing position, otherwise 0. | defender |
| midfielder | Midfielder | integer | 1 when midfielder is a recorded playing position, otherwise 0. | midfielder |
| forward | Forward | integer | 1 when forward is a recorded playing position, otherwise 0. | forward |
| count_tournaments | Tournament Count | integer | Number of tournaments in the row’s tournament, team or stage scope. | count_tournaments |
| list_tournaments | List Tournaments | string | Recorded list of tournament editions associated with the person. | list_tournaments |
| player_wikipedia_link | Player Wikipedia Link | string | Wikipedia reference for player. | player_wikipedia_link |

### Keys

Primary Keys: key_id
Display Key: family_name
Incremental Key:

